INT. FAMILY LIVING ROOM - CHRISTMAS EVE

A small tree, tilted. Wrapping paper in drifts. A space heater ticks.

PAPA LUKAS, sixties, in a Santa hat, stands with a plate of cookies. UNCLE SANDOR, fifties, wedged in an armchair, nurses a beer. COUSIN BEA, twelve, cross-legged on the floor, sorts presents. COUSIN TEDDY, nine, hides behind the couch with a water gun.

PAPA LUKAS
(to the room)
Everybody, cookies.

UNCLE SANDOR
He's making them again, Lukas. Stop him.

PAPA LUKAS
Who is "he"?

UNCLE SANDOR
Teddy! Behind the couch!

TEDDY
(popping up)
I'm not!

He fires. A jet of water hits Sandor in the face. Sandor roars, lunges, tangles in the lamp cord, topples the lamp. Bea and Lukas dive for it together; both catch it at the same moment and freeze.

BEA
Papa, we're the best team.

PAPA LUKAS
(muttering)
We're a disaster.

He sets the lamp upright. Sandor, dripping, glares at Teddy.

UNCLE SANDOR
You're in trouble, nephew.

TEDDY
It's Christmas!

UNCLE SANDOR
Then Santa's bringing you coal.

Teddy bursts into laughter. Bea joins. Papa Lukas holds out the plate, and Sandor, dripping, takes a cookie.
